<# Sans-serif variant, conventional for engineering roles.

   Helvetica via psnfss ships in texlive-fonts-recommended, which the render
   image already installs -- no new package in the Dockerfile. The \sfdefault
   override is required because the helvet package only *provides* the family;
   it does not make it the document default.

   Sans-serif is a presentation choice with no extraction penalty: what matters
   for parsing is the ToUnicode map, which glyphtounicode handles identically
   for both families. #>
<% extends "_base.tex.j2" %>

<% block fontsize %>10pt<% endblock %>

<% block fontpackage %>
\usepackage[scaled=0.92]{helvet}
\renewcommand{\familydefault}{\sfdefault}
<% endblock %>

<% block margintop %>0.5in<% endblock %>
<% block marginbottom %>0.5in<% endblock %>
<% block bulletindent %>0.16in<% endblock %>
